Reduce heapster's memory usage/leaks. As experienced while validating #12243, heapster is OOM'ing way too quickly, and using a surprising amount of memory in general. In that particular case, it OOM'ed after 15 minutes on a 5 node cluster with only a handful of pods running. We need to get it under control so that it can run reliably on larger clusters.

You're free to close this if you feel that it should only be tracked in heapster's repo, but it's an issue that affects kubernetes pretty seriously as well.

@vishh

Add a simple cache for objects stored in etcd.. This is exactly the same as #7288 with a subtle difference in EtcdHelper.

Previously we were using [INLINE_CODE]. As a result if we copied EtcdHelper we had two separate mutexes guarding the same map (map is not deep-copied). This introduced a data-race in integration tests. New version uses [INLINE_CODE] which is also not deep-copied which solves the race.

